+Concise Bounded Description
+---------------------------
+
+:meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd` returns the *Concise Bounded Description*
+of a resource: a new Graph containing the triples that have the resource
+as their subject, following blank node objects recursively and including
+any reified statements about the resource, as defined in the
+`W3C member submission <https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/>`_::
+
+   >>> from rdflib import Graph, URIRef, Literal
+   >>> g = Graph()
+   >>> alice = URIRef("http://example.org/alice")
+   >>> bob = URIRef("http://example.org/bob")
+   >>> knows = URIRef("http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/knows")
+   >>> name = URIRef("http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name")
+   >>> g.add((alice, name, Literal("Alice")))
+   >>> g.add((alice, knows, bob))
+   >>> g.add((bob, name, Literal("Bob")))
+
+   >>> cbd = g.cbd(alice)
+   >>> len(cbd)
+   2
+
+The source graph is not modified.
+
